1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:08,400
Priya: Alright everyone, let's get started. We need to cover the Q3 roadmap, the infra migration, and the API rate limiting issue blocking the mobile team.

2
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:14,600
Marcus: Before we dive in — the staging environment went down again this morning. Eggomelette, did you get a chance to look at that?

3
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:21,800
Eggomelette: Yeah, it was a misconfigured nginx reverse proxy after the last deployment. I've pushed a fix but someone needs to verify it in prod before end of day.

4
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:25,100
Priya: Marcus, can you own the prod verification? Let's target 5 PM today.

5
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:27,000
Marcus: Sure, I'll handle it.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,600
Priya: Good. On Q3 — the exec team has prioritised the payments module, the customer self-serve dashboard, and a performance audit on the checkout flow.

7
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:42,300
Lena: I've been working on the payments module spec. We need to decide between Stripe and Braintree. I sent a comparison doc but haven't heard back from the stakeholders.

8
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:49,400
Priya: Lena, can you set up a 30-minute call with the finance team by Thursday? We need to lock in the payment provider before sprint planning on Monday.

9
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,800
Lena: Got it. I'll send the calendar invite today.

10
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:59,100
Eggomelette: Worth flagging — if we go with Stripe, we'll need to rebuild the webhook infrastructure. Current setup can't handle Stripe's retry logic. I'd need about a week if Stripe is confirmed.

11
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,400
Priya: Can you have a design doc ready by Friday EOD so we can review before committing?

12
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:04,500
Eggomelette: Yes, I'll have it done by Friday.

13
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:11,800
Priya: On the self-serve dashboard — we've approved two contractors. Lena, you're the point of contact. Can you make sure they have Figma access, design system docs, and the API sandbox by Thursday?

14
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,200
Lena: Absolutely, I'll sort that by Thursday.

15
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:21,600
Eggomelette: The API sandbox is still running on mock data from February. Before the contractors hit it, someone needs to reseed it with realistic data or they'll build against broken assumptions.

16
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:25,400
Priya: Eggomelette, can you own the sandbox refresh? Contractors onboard Thursday, so Wednesday is the hard deadline.

17
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:28,100
Eggomelette: If I start tomorrow I can have it done by Wednesday. Not complex, just time-consuming.

18
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:35,600
Lena: On the performance audit — our last Lighthouse scores on the checkout flow were 54 on mobile. The biggest culprits are unoptimised images and a blocking analytics script.

19
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:42,800
Priya: Marcus, can you scope what we can fix on our side — image optimisation, lazy loading — and have a report by next Wednesday?

20
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:46,200
Marcus: Yes. I'll loop in Eggomelette on the server-side render times too since that's his area.

21
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:51,100
Eggomelette: SSR cold start times are spiking — I suspect it's the new middleware chain from the last release. I'll investigate and report back by Wednesday.

22
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:58,400
Lena: Last thing — the mobile team is hitting 429 errors on the product listing endpoint during peak hours. It's causing significant app degradation.

23
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:06,300
Eggomelette: I looked into this. We're applying rate limits per IP, but the mobile app routes everything through a shared API gateway. The entire user base is sharing one bucket — that's the root cause.

24
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:12,200
Marcus: We need per-user token rate limiting. Eggomelette, could you prototype JWT-based rate limiting with Redis?

25
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:18,600
Eggomelette: Yes, I can have a demo-ready prototype in a feature branch by Friday. I'd propose JWT-based limits with Redis as the backend.

26
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:22,800
Priya: Make that official — JWT rate limiting prototype by Friday. High priority.

27
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:28,600
Marcus: Lena, can you message the mobile-dev Slack channel today explaining the root cause and our timeline?

28
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:30,800
Lena: Will do, sending that today.

29
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:38,600
Priya: Alright — Marcus, prod verification today and performance scope by next Wednesday. Lena, payments call by Thursday, contractor access by Thursday, and mobile Slack message today. Eggomelette, sandbox refresh by Wednesday, webhook design doc by Friday, JWT prototype by Friday, and SSR investigation by Wednesday. Thanks everyone.

30
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,400
Marcus: Thanks all. Eggomelette has a full plate.

31
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:43,600
Eggomelette: I'll need a lot of coffee.

32
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:46,000
Lena: We appreciate you. Bye everyone!
